{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>May Reuben live.</b> Even though Reuben chose across the Jordan, which is not the land of YHWH, as it says: וְאַךְ אִם טְמֵאָה אֶרֶץ אֲחֻזַּתְכֶם (Joshua 22:19), and for this reason it is not so prepared for attaining eternal life therein — nevertheless, may he live alone forever." "<b>And let him not die, and let his men be numbered.</b> And let him not die in this world, so that his people be few — like וַאֲנִי מְתֵי מִסְפָּר (Genesis 34:30) — even though it is written לְמַעַן יִרְבּוּ יְמֵיכֶם עַל הָאֲדָמָה (Deuteronomy 11:21)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:31.055239331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}